{"parentUuid":"284ff4ce-f057-4ed3-8f4f-815b6861223f","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"d051cd75-4148-4dde-a96c-1a2da307cda0","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"a73851d","slug":"iridescent-crunching-sunbeam","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_vrtx_01QnYBRiydaT3YFtBy4hFSYY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me provide you with a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Network.json Structure Summary\n\n### 1. Top-Level Keys\n\nThe JSON file contains the following top-level keys:\n- **name**: \"real_world_network\"\n- **description**: \"Power system network\"\n- **baseMVA**: 100.0 (system base MVA)\n- **bus**: Array of bus data\n- **gen**: Array of generator data\n- **branch**: Array of transmission branch data\n- **gencost**: Array of generation cost data\n- **reserve_capacity**: Array of reserve capacity per generator\n- **reserve_requirement**: System reserve requirement value (3697.5 MW)\n- **column_info**: Metadata describing all fields in each data table\n\n### 2. Fields/Columns for Each Data Table\n\n#### **BUS** (13 columns)\n0. BUS_I - bus number (1-indexed)\n1. BUS_TYPE - 1=PQ, 2=PV, 3=Slack\n2. PD - real power demand (MW)\n3. QD - reactive power demand (MVAr)\n4. GS - shunt conductance\n5. BS - shunt susceptance\n6. BUS_AREA - area number\n7. VM - voltage magnitude (pu)\n8. VA - voltage angle (degrees)\n9. BASE_KV - base voltage (kV)\n10. ZONE - loss zone\n11. VMAX - max voltage (pu)\n12. VMIN - min voltage (pu)\n\n#### **GEN** (10 columns)\n0. GEN_BUS - bus number (1-indexed)\n1. PG - real power output (MW)\n2. QG - reactive power output (MVAr)\n3. QMAX - max reactive power (MVAr)\n4. QMIN - min reactive power (MVAr)\n5. VG - voltage setpoint (pu)\n6. MBASE - machine base (MVA)\n7. GEN_STATUS - 1=in-service, 0=out-of-service\n8. PMAX - max real power output (MW)\n9. PMIN - min real power output (MW)\n\n#### **BRANCH** (13 columns)\n0. F_BUS - from bus (1-indexed)\n1. T_BUS - to bus (1-indexed)\n2. BR_R - resistance (pu)\n3. BR_X - reactance (pu)\n4. BR_B - total line charging susceptance (pu)\n5. RATE_A - MVA rating A (long term)\n6. RATE_B - MVA rating B (short term)\n7. RATE_C - MVA rating C (emergency)\n8. TAP - transformer tap ratio\n9. SHIFT - transformer phase shift (degrees)\n10. BR_STATUS - 1=in-service, 0=out-of-service\n11. ANGMIN - min angle difference (degrees)\n12. ANGMAX - max angle difference (degrees)\n\n#### **GENCOST** (variable columns)\n0. MODEL - 1=piecewise linear, 2=polynomial\n1. STARTUP - startup cost ($)\n2. SHUTDOWN - shutdown cost ($)\n3. NCOST - number of cost coefficients\n4+. COST - cost coefficients (highest order first)\n\n#### **RESERVE_CAPACITY** (1 column per generator)\n- Maximum reserve each generator can provide (MW)\n\n### 3. Element Counts\n\n| Element Type | Count |\n|---|---|\n| **Buses** | 300 |\n| **Generators** | 69 |\n| **Branches** | 411 |\n| **Generation costs** | 69 |\n| **Reserve capacity entries** | 69 |\n\n### 4. baseMVA Value\n\n**baseMVA = 100.0 MW**\n\nThis is the system-wide base power used for per-unit normalization in the power system."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":699,"cache_read_input_tokens":14561,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":699,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXZMmMVLSz7PpqHoNuu92","type":"assistant","uuid":"4f0f602d-db79-4b34-81b0-99325fd81608","timestamp":"2026-01-28T07:11:10.641Z"}
